"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She's\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She's a woman.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She's not<br/>She isn't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It's a book.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's not<br/>It isn't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We are \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We're\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We're brothers.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"We're not<br/>We aren't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They're\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They're friends.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They're not<br/>They aren't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You are\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You're\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You're sisters.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You're not<br/>You aren't\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Demonstratives - Singular and Plural"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Demonstratives point something out.   "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For singular items that are close, you use <span class=\"strong\">this</span>. When something is far, you use <span class=\"strong\">that</span>.   <br />For plural items that are near, you use <span class=\"strong\">these</span>. When something is far, you use <span class=\"strong\">those</span>. <br/> Make the demonstrative negative by adding <span class=\"strong\">not</span> after <span class=\"strong\">to be</span>. You can use a short form. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":\"03\",\"columns\":\"05\",\"cells\":[\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">This</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">That</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">These</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Those</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Affirmative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">This is the invitation.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> That is my jacket.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">These are my sisters.<br/> These people are important.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Those are my friends.<br/> Those two guys are her brothers.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Negative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">This is not the invitation.<br/>This isn't the invitation.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> That is not my jacket.<br/> That isn't my jacket.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> These are not my friends.<br/> These aren't my friends.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\"